# Formatting experiment header; it has no semantic attachment.
requirement FMT-001
# Preserve this comment in place.
title: Monotonic evaluation
allocation: Timing service
statement:
  While monitoring an active vehicle, the timing service shall evaluate the
  command-link state at the instants defined by the following expression.

  math latex
    k^\ast = \min\left\{k \in \{0,1,2,\ldots\} \mid
      t_0 + k T_{\mathrm{eval}} - t_{\mathrm{last}} \ge T_{\mathrm{loss}}\right\}

    T_{\mathrm{eval}} \le 0.10\,\mathrm{s}
  end math

  The symbols retain their definitions from the project timing glossary.
rationale:
  Explicit evaluation instants make the threshold boundary reviewable without
  requiring a renderer.
source: SRC-SAFETY-001, revision B
decomposes: FMT-003
end requirement

# This inter-record comment remains surrounded by exactly these blank lines.


requirement FMT-002
title: Operator notification
statement:
  Within 500 ms after command-link loss is declared, the operator interface
  shall display the active vehicle identifier and declaration time.
# These relationships retain their authored order.
decomposes: FMT-001
decomposes: FMT-003
end requirement

requirement FMT-003
title: Safe recovery
statement:
  The mission-control system shall initiate safe recovery after command-link
  loss.
end requirement
# Formatting experiment trailer.
